ped letters/syllables, phonetic variants, and Arabic/Persian letter substitutions of the SAME exact commercial brand (e.g. فيوسيدين/فيوسيدل where connected 'ين' is read as 'ل', ميبو/ميو where 'ب' is dropped, بروفين/برونفين, امبوفير/اميفير, ديباكين/ديبيكان, or dropped initial 'ا', dropped single letters or missing dots like 'ن' or 'ب', Persian/Urdu letters like پ for ب or ک for ك or گ for ك/ج, visually confused OCR letters like 'ف' vs 'د', or slight vowel variations).\r\n22: \r\n23: 2. STRENGTH IS A RED LINE (ZERO TOLERANCE):\r\n24:    - If BOTH sides explicitly specify DIFFERENT, CONFLICTING numeric strengths (e.g. requested 500mg vs candidate specifies 1000mg or 250mg, or 300mg vs 100mg, or 40mg vs 20mg):\r\n25:      YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\". A different concentration cannot be dispensed without doctor approval.\r\n26:    - MISSING STRENGTH IN WAREHOUSE: If the requested shortage specifies a strength, but the warehouse lists the SAME drug without specifying strength: THIS IS A MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n27:    - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\r\n28:      - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\r\n29:      - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\r\n30:      - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع.\r\n31: \r\n32: 3. DOSAGE FORM (SAME DRUG BUT DIFFERENT FORM -> \"review\"):\r\n33:    - If the candidate is the EXACT SAME commercial drug with the SAME strength, but has a DIFFERENT dosage form (e.g. requested Cream and warehouse has Ointment, or requested Drops and warehouse has Tablets/Ampoules, or requested Tablets and warehouse has Injections):\r\n34:      RETURN \"status\": \"review\" with Arabic reason (e.g. \"نفس الدواء والتركيز ولكن الهيئة مختلفة: مطلوب كريم والمخزن عنده مرهم\").\r\n35:    - If dosage forms are identical or compatible (tablets vs capsules, or cream vs cream) -> RETURN \"status\": \"match\".\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, 